# The Docker build context is uploaded to the daemon whole, whatever the Dockerfile
# COPYs, so this keeps secrets, private notes and bulk out of it. The image itself
# gets only what the Dockerfile names: pyproject.toml, README.md, LICENSE and src/
# (hatchling's metadata needs the readme and the license file to build the wheel, so
# those three must NOT be listed here).

# Secrets and private notes -- never in a context, never in an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.md

# Version control, tooling, local environments and caches.
.git
.github
.claude
.venv
**/.venv
node_modules
**/node_modules
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Other parts of the repo: the API image runs none of them.
web
extension
tests
docs
latex-service
supabase
scripts
